e-retention-eol walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the Aster Diagnostics retention + destruction schedule, legal-hold
procedure, and decommissioning checklist, authored and self-reviewed in-session.

Scope: fictional Aster Diagnostics (continued); five data types from the lifecycle
lesson. All company facts and all legal bases labeled as EXAMPLE bases (a fictional
company cannot cite real statutes honestly).
Artifacts authored:
  - Retention + destruction schedule: period, basis (example), computable trigger,
    disposition w/ 800-88r2 method + verification, EOL/EOSL note per row
  - Legal-hold procedure: declared by general counsel (CEO fallback); written notice
    to custodians within 48h; written acknowledgment; automated destruction suspended;
    quarterly hold review; written release w/ resumption basis
  - Decommissioning checklist, 7 steps: migrate/destroy (method+verification) ->
    backups scheduled -> credentials revoked -> CMDB retired w/ history -> licenses
    reclaimed -> physical disposition per 800-88r2 -> verifier sign-off
  - Schedule-governs-itself row: destruction records 7y; hold docs hold+6y
Design decisions recorded in lesson §3:
  1. Triggers must be computable events ("7y from last encounter", not "7 years")
  2. Example bases labeled honestly; real deployment cites actual authorities
  3. EOSL tracked in CMDB; migration planning starts 12 months out; EOSL-in-production
     = risk acceptance w/ owner+date or migration date, nothing between
  4. Governance artifacts get schedule rows too

